  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Syria - Strengthened Protection against violence, Coercion and Deliberate Deprivation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened Protection against violence, Coercion and Deliberate Deprivation in Syria: Syria remains in a protracted humanitarian crisis after 13 years of conflict, with around 16.7 million people in need of assistance and over 90% are estimated to live in poverty. The health system is overwhelmed, with widespread infrastructure damage, disease outbreaks, and limited access to care&#x2014;particularly for women, children, and displaced populations. Protection risks are severe, including violence against health workers, SGBV, and restricted movement across conflict lines. Norwegian Red Cross (NoRC), in partnership with the Syrian Arab Red Crescent (SARC), aims to reach highly vulnerable individuals through support to integrated healthcare services, emergency response, WASH interventions, and protection, including strengthening of referral pathways. The initiative prioritises locally led humanitarian action and enhancing community resilience through sustainable and inclusive approaches.</narrative>
  </description>
